@yegor256 In your example `sourceDir` is not a collection, it's a `File`. 

I checked [Surefire Plugin sources](https://github.com/apache/maven-surefire/blob/0e5de8f9f1351c6e88c31cff99fb7600e86ffe07/maven-surefire-plugin/src/main/java/org/apache/maven/plugin/surefire/SurefirePlugin.java#L212) as an example of such properties: 
```
@Parameter( property = "surefire.includes" )
// TODO use regex for fully qualified class names in 3.0 and change the filtering abilities
private List<String> includes;
```

It uses `property` argument and defaults are defined explicitly in the code:
```
@Override
protected String[] getDefaultIncludes()
{
    return new String[]{ "**/Test*.java", "**/*Test.java", "**/*Tests.java", "**/*TestCase.java" };
}

if ( asScanList && includes.isEmpty() )
{
    addAll( includes, getDefaultIncludes() );
}
```
And I believe the intention is to set this property within `<configuration>` tag for the plugin - not `-D` parameters.
Maybe we can do the same way?

