@volodya-lombrozo Before you identified this problem, I didn't even think about it and didn't have a problem with it. 
EO is something that should live without knowing about java, copiler, tojos and so on. We actually already have such mappings from EO to our compiler: `@` -> `ф`, `^` -> `σ`, ... now there's one more `|` -> `#`. I don't see any problem here and don't see the reason for this ticket, at least for now. 
P.S. And we should remember that `|` is invalid for file naming on windows. That's why it was changed to `#`

@yegor256  @maxonfjvipon 
1. As for `@` -> `ф`, `^` -> `σ` symbols: We use this mapping to connect the frontend with phi-calculus (please correct me if I'm wrong), so I can understand the rationale behind it.
2. As for `|` and `#` - they are solutions to the problem with "Windows paths." Why does Windows influence our architecture and code that isn't related to Windows at all? Writing comments isn't a solution at all. I'm more than sure that I'm not the only one who will face this confusion. What do I suggest? Let's use `|` everywhere; it's understandable and easy to maintain. If we have problems with Windows paths, then we should address them where we save data to the filesystem. In other words, right now, Windows is dictating our architecture, which is incorrect. It's better to change direction: our architecture should take precedence.

